\frac{3}{11}&=0.{3}\underline{0}{0}\underline{9}\underline{0}{7}\underline{2}\underline{7}\underline{2}{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\underline{5}\underline{4}\\
&=0.\underbrace{2727\dots}_{\text{the digits 27 repeat}} \end{align*}
So $a=2$ and $b=7$ , and their sum is $\boxed{9}$ .</think> <answer> 9 </answer>

